gh-runner-ctl(8)

# NAME

gh-runner-ctl - manage rootless ephemeral GitHub Actions runners

# SYNOPSIS

*gh-runner-ctl* _command_ [_id_] [options]

# DESCRIPTION

*gh-runner-ctl* is a thin wrapper that runs *systemctl --user* and *podman* as
the *gh-runner* service account with the correct *XDG_RUNTIME_DIR* and
*DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS*. Encapsulating that awkwardness is the whole reason
the command exists; an operator should never have to think about it.

Must be run as root, or as the service account itself.

*/etc/gh-runner/instances.d/* is the only store. There is no database, no
cache, and no registry file. Generated unit drop-ins and the Podman secret are
derived state, regenerated by *sync*, never a second source of truth.
Hand-editing a conf file and running *sync* is fully equivalent to going
through this tool; *add* is a scaffolding convenience, not a requirement.

# COMMANDS

*add* _id_ *--url* _URL_ [*--labels* _L_] [*--name* _N_] [*--group* _G_]
	Scaffold */etc/gh-runner/instances.d/*_id_*.conf*. Does not start
	anything.

*show* _id_
	Effective configuration with global and instance files merged, grouped by
	where each key actually goes. Warns about values Podman will accept and
	misinterpret.

*edit* _id_
	Open the conf file in *$EDITOR* and validate on save.

*rm* _id_ [*--purge*]
	Disable and remove the instance. State under */var/lib/gh-runner/*_id_ is
	kept unless *--purge* is given.

*enable* _id_ [*--now*]
	Clear any drain marker, regenerate the drop-in, enable and start.
	Refuses if there is no credential, rather than letting the instance enter
	a restart loop against a missing secret.

*disable* [_id_ | *--all*] [*--now*]
	Without *--now*, marks the instance for *drain*: the current job finishes,
	the container exits, and nothing restarts it. With *--now*, stops the unit
	immediately and kills any running job.

*sync*
	Reconcile all derived state to the conf files: Quadlet symlinks, unit
	drop-ins, orphan drop-ins, and the Podman secret. Idempotent. This is the
	integration point for configuration management — template *instances.d/*,
	call *sync*, done.

*list*
	Conf files against enabled units, with drift and drain state marked.

*status*
	Per-instance active state and restart count.

*doctor*
	Check the things that fail silently. See *DIAGNOSTICS*.

*set-credential* [*--stdin*]
	Write */etc/gh-runner/credentials* with mode 0600 and load it into the
	Podman secret *gh-runner-token*.

*check-credential*
	Verify the credential can mint a registration token for each configured
	*RUNNER_URL*.

# DRAINING

Neither systemd verb does what is wanted for a graceful stop: *disable* only
affects the next boot and leaves the restart loop running, while *stop* kills
the in-flight job.

*disable* without *--now* therefore writes */var/lib/gh-runner/*_id_*/.drain*.
The container entrypoint checks for it before registering and exits 78; the
unit carries *RestartPreventExitStatus=78*, so *Restart=always* declines and
the instance settles at a job boundary with nothing half-finished. A container
already running a job is untouched and drains on its own.

*list* reports such an instance as *draining*, since "enabled, not running, on
purpose" is otherwise indistinguishable from a crash loop that has given up.

# DIAGNOSTICS

*doctor* checks, in order: the service account, linger, subuid/subgid,
*podman.socket*, host Podman version against the image's client, cgroup
controller delegation, the credential and its secret, Quadlet symlinks,
*quadlet -dryrun*, stray *:Z* volume options, and per-instance config
including duplicate *RUNNER_NAME*.

Every one of these corresponds to a failure that presents as something other
than its cause. Malformed Quadlet keys fail silently; a non-Quadlet file in
the Quadlet directory is ignored outright; a missing *podman.socket* surfaces
as an unrelated Podman error; an undelegated controller yields a limit that is
configured, reported by *systemctl show*, and not enforced.

# FILES

/etc/gh-runner/gh-runner.conf
	Global defaults.

/etc/gh-runner/instances.d/_id_.conf
	Per-instance configuration. The only store.

/etc/gh-runner/credentials
	GitHub credential, mode 0600. Source of truth for the Podman secret.

/etc/systemd/user/gh-runner@_id_.service.d/limits.conf
	Generated. Do not edit; edit the conf file and run *sync*.

/var/lib/gh-runner/_id_/
	Instance state: the synced runner tree, *_work*, *_diag*, and the drain
	marker.

# SECURITY

This is not a security boundary. The runner container holds the host Podman
socket, so anything running inside it can drive every container on the box,
including mounting arbitrary host paths. The VM is the boundary. Do not attach
these runners to public repositories.

All instances share one uid and one Podman store, so they are one trust
domain. Instance 2 can inspect instance 3's job containers.

# SEE ALSO

*gh-runner.conf*(5), *podman*(1), *quadlet*(5), *systemctl*(1)
